From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ninjacornix <milanvrankic@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:16:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(editor): title bar names the project

Joinery-only, not for upstream. The title bar read "visual.tscn - Harbour Keeper", repeating the scene tab beside it. In Joinery's layout it shows the project's name alone; the scene tab already names the scene and its unsaved mark. The OS window title keeps the scene so the task bar still tells windows apart.
---
 editor/editor_node.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/editor/editor_node.cpp b/editor/editor_node.cpp
index 851fe73..c17da57 100644
--- a/editor/editor_node.cpp
+++ b/editor/editor_node.cpp
@@ -379,7 +379,9 @@ void EditorNode::_update_title() {
 	}
 	DisplayServer::get_singleton()->window_set_title(title + String(" - ") + GODOT_VERSION_NAME);
 	if (project_title) {
-		project_title->set_text(title);
+		// Joinery: the scene tab already names the scene and its unsaved mark,
+		// so the title bar shows the project alone.
+		project_title->set_text(EditorSettings::is_joinery_layout() ? (appname.is_empty() ? TTR("Unnamed Project") : appname) : title);
 	}
 }
 
